# CODEOWNERS
# Each line is a file pattern followed by one or more owners.
#
# Policy (from PR #615, which this file is based on and supersedes): routine
# PRs — dependency bumps, i18n, docs, app-code features — merge unattended
# once required status checks are green. Only the paths listed below require
# human code-owner review before merge; everything else is intentionally left
# uncovered so it keeps auto-merging. There is deliberately NO catch-all `*`
# rule: adding one would gate every PR again and defeat the fleet entirely.
#
# This file is now LOAD-BEARING, not advisory. It is the whole of the fleet's
# "this needs a human" gate. The orchestrator used to make that call itself
# (`classifyImpact` + `mayAutoMerge`), on the operator's laptop, before the PR
# existed — so GitHub never knew, and anyone could merge past it. Every path
# in `HIGH_IMPACT_PATHS` (orchestrator/src/impact.ts) is therefore owned here,
# and tests/orchestrator/guards.test.ts fails if one of them ever stops being
# covered. Requires the ruleset's `required_code_owner_review` to be on; until
# that is enabled these lines request review but do not block.
#
# Consequence worth calling out, inherited from #615: GitHub Actions
# dependency bumps (Dependabot PRs touching .github/workflows/) require
# review, because a compromised or malicious action is a supply-chain vector.

# ─── Crypto, protocol, and the key boundaries around them ──────────────
packages/crypto/                    @rhonda-rodododo
packages/protocol/schemas/          @rhonda-rodododo
packages/protocol/crypto-labels.json @rhonda-rodododo
packages/shared/crypto-labels.ts    @rhonda-rodododo

# Not the crypto crate itself, but the surfaces that keep (or could leak) a
# device private key: the webview IPC boundary, the Tauri permission grants,
# and the iOS/Android Keychain/Keystore wrappers.
src/client/lib/platform.ts          @rhonda-rodododo
apps/desktop/src/crypto.rs          @rhonda-rodododo
apps/desktop/capabilities/          @rhonda-rodododo
apps/ios/Sources/Services/CryptoService.swift @rhonda-rodododo
apps/android/app/src/main/java/org/llamenos/hotline/crypto/ @rhonda-rodododo
apps/android/keystore               @rhonda-rodododo

